          },
          "text": "‼️Let this stay here on the record. Today, on 26 August @OpenAI retired the o3 model that was supposed to be available throughout August for all paid accounts as advertised. Except it wasn't - they've stopped serving o3 between 9-10 August and they never ever fixed it. \n\nPeople were sending emails to support every single day only to find their cases being totally dismissed and unanswered. People raised the same complaints daily on Reddit and X only to be ignored and mocked by OAI staff (the mockery itself is the proof they were fully aware that o3 was unavailable but decided to do nothing about it except make fun of the model and their own paying customers).  \n\nTo anyone saying this doesn't matter because not many people interacted with o3 - you are so wrong. \n\nIf you think @OpenAI won't do this again to any model of your choice, codex or any other 'product' they ship - think again. This is the lab that operates in broad daylight however they chose to operate. They have normalised lying, rug pulling, bait and switching and public shaming. They have proven again and again they can never be trusted. This is the lab that says: \"OpenAI’s mission is to ensure that artificial general intelligence benefits all of humanity\". The humanity should be very worried. \n\n@sama @gdb @thsottiaux @ajambrosino shame on you, fraudsters."
        },
